.dart_tool/
.packages
build/
pubspec.lock
*.iml
.idea/
.vscode/
*.g.dart
.forge/

ztmp/

# Flutter host-specific generated tooling — regenerated by `flutter pub get`
# on every host (absolute pub-cache paths, host Flutter version, build env), so
# tracking them produces per-host churn that breaks fleet reconcile. Flutter's
# own templates already mark these "do not check into version control".
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/Flutter/ephemeral/
**/flutter/ephemeral/

# Test run logs, baselines and analysis — machine-generated, never versioned.
# These live in a `testlog/` folder next to each project's `doc/` folder.
# The `doc/` folder itself is fully tracked (no test artifacts written there).
**/testlog/

# Retired build state (build_tom build_cleanup7): the build number lives in
# version.versioner.dart; an old buildkit that still writes this file is ignored.
tom_build_state.json
